IMPORT prelude

-- Professional Engineers Act 1991 (Singapore) -- who may do, sign, offer and supply professional engineering work and use the title
-- (ss 15, 17, 18, 19, 20 and the Schedule), compulsory voting (s 5), removal and re-registration (ss 26, 27), practising certificate
-- deadlines (s 28), disciplinary sanctions and when they bite (ss 50, 51), offence penalties (ss 15(10), 17(2), 54(6), 58) and the
-- Board's immunity (s 63).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PEA1991.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 15 of 2026 (s 21(2A), (2B), in force 1 January 2026) and Act 25 of 2024 (in force 1 October 2025) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions an engineer, a firm, a
-- builder or a client meets. Not encoded: the Board's constitution and procedure (ss 4, 6-14), registration qualifications (s 21,
-- which turn on examinations and experience "prescribed by the Board"), specialist registration (s 22), multidiscipline and
-- corporate practice licensing (Part 6), the complaint and investigation machinery (ss 39-49), investigators' powers beyond the
-- offence in s 54(6), corporate officer liability (ss 59, 60), rules and exemptions (ss 61, 62).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Professional Engineers Act 1991 -- practice`

§§ `2, 3, 15, 19, 20 -- the actor`

-- s 2: "prescribed branch of professional engineering work" means chemical, civil, electrical or mechanical engineering, or any other
-- branch prescribed. The branch is not modelled; every field below is about THE branch in question.
-- s 3(1): "Nothing in this Act applies to anything done or omitted to be done by the Government or by a public officer under the
-- Government's authority."
-- s 20(2): nothing in the Act prevents a person "not registered under this Act and who is a member of any class of persons specified
-- in the Schedule from carrying on any activity which the person is authorised to carry out under any written law". The Schedule:
-- certificated officers under the Merchant Shipping Act 1995; holders of WSH certificates of competency for steam boilers or internal
-- combustion engines; electrical workers licensed under the Electricity Act 2001; fire safety engineers registered under the Fire
-- Safety Act 1993.
-- s 50(10): while a suspension order is in force the person "is not ... to be regarded as having in force a practising certificate".
DECLARE Actor HAS
    `is the Government or a public officer acting under its authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a registered professional engineer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a practising certificate for the branch` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is suspended from practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works under the direction or supervision of a certificated engineer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a foreign engineer authorised by the Board to collaborate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a licensed practice for the branch` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is winding up a licensed practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a partnership wholly of certificated engineers, one authorised for the branch` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts on own account, for a licensed practice, or as partner in such a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an allied professional offering only as partner in a licensed partnership or LLP` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in a Schedule class acting within its written-law authority` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds a practising certificate in force for the branch` IF
        `the actor`'s `is a registered professional engineer`
    AND `the actor`'s `has a practising certificate for the branch`
    AND (NOT `the actor`'s `is suspended from practice`)

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is outside the Act or saved by section 20(2)` IF
        `the actor`'s `is the Government or a public officer acting under its authority`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is in a Schedule class acting within its written-law authority`

§§ `15(1), 19 -- engaging in the work`

-- s 15(1): a person "must not, in Singapore, engage in any of the prescribed branches of professional engineering work, or draw or
-- prepare any plan, sketch, drawing, design, specification or other document" relating to it, unless the person (a) is a registered
-- professional engineer with a practising certificate for that branch; (b) "is working under the direction or supervision of" such a
-- person; (c) being a foreign engineer, is authorised by the Board to work "in collaboration with" such a person; (d) is a licensed
-- professional engineering practice for that branch; or (e) is a partnership consisting wholly of certificated engineers, one or more
-- of whom is authorised for that branch.
-- s 19: nothing prevents an unregistered person "from carrying out work in respect of the construction of or repairs to any building
-- ... in any case in which plans are not required by any written law to be submitted to a building authority".
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor, `the work is building work needing no plans` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may engage in the branch of work` IF
        `is outside the Act or saved by section 20(2)` `the actor`
    OR  `the work is building work needing no plans`
    OR  `holds a practising certificate in force for the branch` `the actor`
    OR  `the actor`'s `works under the direction or supervision of a certificated engineer`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is a foreign engineer authorised by the Board to collaborate`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is a licensed practice for the branch`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is a partnership wholly of certificated engineers, one authorised for the branch`

§§ `15(3) -- signing and submitting to a building authority`

-- s 15(3): a person must not sign and submit to a building authority or public authority any plan or other document relating to a
-- prescribed branch, or any report or certificate "required by any written law to be signed by a professional engineer", "unless the
-- person is a registered professional engineer who has in force a practising certificate"; "and any document that is signed in
-- contravention of this subsection is INVALID".
-- Narrower than s 15(1): the supervised assistant, the authorised foreign engineer and the licensed practice may all do the work, but
-- none of them may sign it.
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sign and submit to a building authority` IF
        `is outside the Act or saved by section 20(2)` `the actor`
    OR  `holds a practising certificate in force for the branch` `the actor`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signed document is invalid` IF
    NOT `may sign and submit to a building authority` `the actor`

§§ `15(4), (5) -- titles`

-- s 15(4): a person must not use "(a) the words 'professional engineer' or any additions to or abbreviation or derivative of those
-- words in connection with the person's designation; (b) the word 'engineer' or the abbreviation 'Er.' or 'Engr.' as a title before
-- the person's name; or (c) any word ... that will lead to the belief that the person is a registered professional engineer, unless
-- the person is a registered professional engineer."
-- The condition is REGISTRATION, not a practising certificate: a registered engineer without a certificate (or suspended) may still
-- use the title.
-- s 15(5): a foreign engineer authorised under s 15(1)(c) may be allowed "such addition to or derivative of the words 'professional
-- engineer' as may be approved by the Board".
DECLARE Title IS ONE OF
    `"Er." before the name`
    `"Engineer" before the name`
    `"professional engineer" as a designation`
    `a Board-approved derivative of "professional engineer"`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor, `the title` IS A Title
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may use the title` IF
        `the actor`'s `is the Government or a public officer acting under its authority`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is a registered professional engineer`
    OR  CONSIDER `the title`
        WHEN `a Board-approved derivative of "professional engineer"` THEN `the actor`'s `is a foreign engineer authorised by the Board to collaborate`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `15(6) to (9) -- holding out, supplying and offering services`

-- s 15(6): a person must not advertise or hold out as authorised to supply professional engineering services in a prescribed branch
-- unless (a) a certificated engineer for that branch, (b) a licensed practice for that branch, or (c) a partnership wholly of
-- certificated engineers. (7) "Nothing in subsection (6) prevents a licensed professional engineering practice from carrying on any
-- activity necessary to the winding up of that practice."
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may hold out as authorised to supply services` IF
        `is outside the Act or saved by section 20(2)` `the actor`
    OR  `holds a practising certificate in force for the branch` `the actor`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is a licensed practice for the branch`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is winding up a licensed practice`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is a partnership wholly of certificated engineers, one authorised for the branch`

-- s 15(8)(a): a person must not SUPPLY services unless (i) a licensed practice for the branch, or (ii) a certificated engineer for the
-- branch doing so "(A) on the person's own account or as a director, partner or employee ... of a licensed professional engineering
-- practice ... or (B) as a partner in a partnership consisting wholly of registered professional engineers".
-- (b): a person must not OFFER to supply unless (i) a person in (a); (ii) "an allied professional who is doing so only by reason of
-- being a partner in a licensed partnership or licensed limited liability partnership"; or (iii) a foreign engineer authorised under
-- s 15(1)(c).
-- The authorised foreign engineer and the allied professional may OFFER but are not listed among those who may SUPPLY.
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may supply services` IF
        `is outside the Act or saved by section 20(2)` `the actor`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is a licensed practice for the branch`
    OR  (    `holds a practising certificate in force for the branch` `the actor`
         AND `the actor`'s `acts on own account, for a licensed practice, or as partner in such a partnership`)

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may offer to supply services` IF
        `may supply services` `the actor`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is an allied professional offering only as partner in a licensed partnership or LLP`
    OR  `the actor`'s `is a foreign engineer authorised by the Board to collaborate`

-- s 15(9): "Despite subsection (8), a builder may in connection with any building works which the builder undertakes to carry out,
-- supply or offer to supply" services if (a) they are provided by a person in s 15(8)(a); or (b) they are (i) provided by a
-- certificated engineer EMPLOYED BY THE BUILDER and (ii) "relate to any of the prescribed works necessary for the progress of the
-- building works".
GIVEN `provided by a person within section 15(8)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN, `provided by a certificated engineer employed by the builder` IS A BOOLEAN, `relate to prescribed works necessary for the building works` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the builder may supply the services with its building works` IF
        `provided by a person within section 15(8)(a)`
    OR  (`provided by a certificated engineer employed by the builder` AND `relate to prescribed works necessary for the building works`)

§§ `15(10), 17(2), 54(6), 58 -- penalties`

-- s 15(10): contravening s 15(1), (3), (4), (6) or (8): (a) a natural person -- fine up to $5,000; a repeat offender up to $10,000 or
-- imprisonment up to 6 months or both; (b) a body corporate -- up to $5,000; a repeat offender up to $10,000 (no imprisonment).
-- (11): a repeat offender has at least one earlier conviction under s 15(10) or the former s 10(6) "(whether before, on or after
-- 15 January 2018)".
GIVEN `is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 15(10)` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat offender` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is available under section 15(10)` IF
    `is a natural person` AND `is a repeat offender`

-- s 17(1): a person must not "employ as a professional engineer any person who is not a registered professional engineer". (2): fine
-- up to $2,000; "in the case of second or subsequent offence", up to $5,000.
GIVEN `employs the person as a professional engineer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employment is an offence under section 17` IF
    `employs the person as a professional engineer` AND (NOT `the person is registered`)

GIVEN `is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 17` MEANS
    IF `is a second or subsequent offence` THEN 5000 ELSE 2000

-- First-offence maxima compared. s 54(6) (resisting or failing to comply with an investigator) and s 58 (falsifying a register,
-- procuring registration, a certificate or a licence by false representation, or aiding either) each carry "a fine not exceeding
-- $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both" from the first offence. Illegal practice under s 15 carries
-- imprisonment only for a repeat natural-person offender.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `illegal practice under section 15`
    `employing an unregistered engineer under section 17`
    `obstructing an investigator under section 54(6)`
    `falsifying a register or procuring registration falsely under section 58`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a first offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `employing an unregistered engineer under section 17` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is available for a first offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an investigator under section 54(6)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `falsifying a register or procuring registration falsely under section 58` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `18 -- fees and refunds`

-- s 18(1): a person "is not entitled to demand, claim or sue for or recover any charge, fee or remuneration" for professional
-- engineering services supplied, or offered, "unless the person supplying or offering to supply ... is authorised by this Act to supply
-- those services".
-- (2): a person who paid another "for that other person engaging in conduct which is in contravention of section 15, may recover the
-- money ... if the person did not know or have reason to believe, when making payment, that the conduct ... was in contravention".
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplier may recover its fee` IF
    `may supply services` `the actor`

GIVEN `paid for conduct contravening section 15` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or had reason to believe it contravened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payer may recover the payment` IF
    `paid for conduct contravening section 15` AND (NOT `knew or had reason to believe it contravened`)

§§ `5 -- compulsory voting`

-- s 5(1): every registered engineer with a practising certificate in force on the day of the Board election "must vote". (2): one who
-- fails to "is not entitled to apply for a practising certificate unless he or she (a) satisfies the Registrar that he or she had a
-- good and sufficient reason for not voting ...; or (b) pays to the Board a penalty prescribed by the Board".
GIVEN `had a practising certificate on election day` IS A BOOLEAN, `voted` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfied the Registrar of a good reason` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid the prescribed penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for a practising certificate after the election` IF
        (NOT `had a practising certificate on election day`)
    OR  `voted`
    OR  `satisfied the Registrar of a good reason`
    OR  `paid the prescribed penalty`

§§ `28 -- practising certificate deadlines`

-- s 28(1): an engineer who wants to practise after 31 December must, "not later than 1 December of that year", apply for a certificate
-- for the succeeding year. (2): a FIRST application after registration "may be made at any time during the year", for the remainder of
-- the year. (5): anyone else who misses the s 28(1) deadline may, "on payment of such additional fee as may be prescribed", be issued
-- a certificate for (a) the succeeding year if applying in December, or (b) the remainder of the year if applying on or after
-- 1 January. (6): a certificate is in force until 31 December of its year.
-- The month and day are of the application; `for the following year` says which year's certificate is sought.
GIVEN `first application after registration` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the following year` IS A BOOLEAN, `month` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an additional fee is payable` IF
    IF `first application after registration`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF `for the following year`
         THEN `month` EQUALS 12 AND `day` GREATER THAN 1
         ELSE TRUE

-- s 28(7): a change of practice address "must be notified ... to the Registrar within 2 weeks of the change".
`days to notify a change of practice address` MEANS 14

§§ `26, 27 -- removal and coming back`

-- s 26(1): the Board may remove an engineer who (a) has no address in Singapore for contact, or (b) "has not renewed his or her
-- practising certificate for a continuous period of at least 10 years". (2): also for fraud or misrepresentation, a withdrawn
-- qualification, or failure to comply with a Disciplinary Committee order under s 50(2)(c) or (e). (5): an engineer may apply to have
-- his or her own name removed; (8) but "No order is to be made" if "(a) disciplinary action is pending against the applicant; or (b)
-- the conduct of the applicant is the subject of an inquiry by an Investigation Committee".
-- s 27(1): a person removed under s 50(2)(a) whose appeal to the High Court is allowed "must ... be immediately reinstated without
-- payment of any fee". (2): the Board may consider a fresh application "after the expiry of at least 3 years from the removal". (3):
-- but a person removed under s 26(1) "may make a fresh application for registration at any time".
-- s 27(2) is written of "any person" removed. Read literally, it covers a person removed at his or her own request under s 26(5).
DECLARE RemovalGround IS ONE OF
    `no contact address in Singapore`
    `certificate not renewed for 10 years`
    `registration obtained by fraud`
    `qualification withdrawn`
    `failure to comply with a disciplinary order`
    `removal ordered by a Disciplinary Committee`
    `own application`

GIVEN `years without renewing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may remove for non-renewal` IF
    `years without renewing` AT LEAST 10

GIVEN `disciplinary action is pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `under Investigation Committee inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may remove on the engineer's own application` IF
    (NOT `disciplinary action is pending`) AND (NOT `under Investigation Committee inquiry`)

GIVEN `the ground` IS A RemovalGround, `years since removal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may consider a fresh application` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `no contact address in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `certificate not renewed for 10 years` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `years since removal` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN `the ground` IS A RemovalGround, `appeal allowed by the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must be reinstated without fee` IF
        `appeal allowed by the High Court`
    AND CONSIDER `the ground`
        WHEN `removal ordered by a Disciplinary Committee` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `50, 51 -- disciplinary sanctions`

-- s 50(2): a Disciplinary Committee may (a) order removal from the register; (b) "suspend ... from practice for a period of not more
-- than 2 years"; (c) "impose ... a penalty not exceeding $50,000"; (d) censure; (e) make any other order. (3): "In addition", costs
-- "not exceeding $50,000".
GIVEN `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER, `penalty` IS A NUMBER, `costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sanction is within section 50` IF
        `months of suspension` AT MOST 24
    AND `penalty` AT MOST 50000
    AND `costs` AT MOST 50000

-- s 50(7): an order under (2) "does not take effect until the expiry of 30 days after the order is made". (8), (9): for removal or
-- suspension the Committee may order it IMMEDIATELY if "necessary for the protection of members of the public or ... in the best
-- interests of" the engineer; such an order "takes effect from the time the order is made".
-- s 51(4): "Despite anything in section 50", where a person has appealed against an order under s 50(2) or (3), "the order does not
-- take effect unless" confirmed, or the appeal is dismissed or withdrawn.
-- `days since the order` counts whole days elapsed; 30 means the 30 days have expired (an inference about counting). An immediate
-- order under s 50(8) is treated as taking effect even if appealed, because s 51(4) speaks of orders "mentioned in section 50(2) or
-- (3)" and the immediate order is made under s 50(8) -- an inference; the text does not say how the two interact.
GIVEN `days since the order` IS A NUMBER, `immediate order under section 50(8)` IS A BOOLEAN, `appeal pending or allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disciplinary order has taken effect` IF
    IF `immediate order under section 50(8)`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `appeal pending or allowed`
         THEN FALSE
         ELSE `days since the order` AT LEAST 30

-- s 50(1)(e): a director, manager, partner or employee of a licensed practice may be disciplined for failing "to take reasonable steps
-- to prevent" the practice acting so as to warrant revocation or a penalty. (11): the engineer is "not to be deemed to have taken
-- reasonable steps ... unless he or she satisfies the Disciplinary Committee that (a) the act was done without his or her knowledge;
-- (b) he or she was not in a position to influence the conduct ...; or (c) he or she, being in such a position, exercised all due
-- diligence".
GIVEN `the act was done without the engineer's knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `not in a position to influence the practice` IS A BOOLEAN, `exercised all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the engineer is taken to have taken reasonable steps` IF
        `the act was done without the engineer's knowledge`
    OR  `not in a position to influence the practice`
    OR  `exercised all due diligence`

§§ `63 -- the Board's immunity`

-- s 63: "No action or proceedings shall lie against the Board, any committee appointed by the Board under this Act, or any member
-- thereof for any act or thing done under this Act unless it is proved to the court that the act or thing was done in bad faith or
-- with malice."
GIVEN `bad faith or malice proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action lies against the Board` IF
    `bad faith or malice proved`
